{{Quote|My dad worked the line at the CEC plant before he got laid off&hellip;He wanted to be a pilot.''"<br />"''You, uh, close with your old man?''"<br />"''Not really.|Han Solo, to Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|<ref name="Solo" />}}
'''Ovan'''<ref name="Han Chewie 1" /> was a [[human]]<ref name="Han Chewie 2" /> [[Gender|male]] who was the [[Parent|father]] of famed [[smuggler]]-turned-[[Alliance to Restore the Republic|rebel]] [[Han Solo]] and the grandfather of [[Ben Solo]]. He lived on [[Corellia]] during Solo's early [[Standard year|years]], where he worked in the [[Corellian Engineering Corporation]] [[shipyard]]s, building [[Starship|vessels]] such as [[YT-1300 light freighter]]s. Han Solo's father wished he could leave Corellia on such a ship, but was never able to afford to.<ref name="Solo" /> At some point, Ovan brought his son to the [[freighter]] [[factory]] where he worked. His father pointed out that the ships being built there were his contributions to [[the galaxy]], but that they ultimately did not matter. His father then advised him that Han was not meant to build ships, but rather to fly them.<ref name="Most Wanted" /> According to Han, who recounted his father's story to [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian]], he was never close with his father.<ref name="Solo" /> Sometime afterwards when Han was young, his father abandoned him<ref name="Solo Expanded Edition">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story: Expanded Edition]]''</ref> and eventually [[Death|died]] in [[24 BBY]].<ref name="Timelines" />

In [[10 BBY]], Han Solo took up the life of a scoundrel.<ref name="Timelines" /> On one mission between [[8 BBY]] and [[2 BBY]],<ref name="HanChewiedate">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of ''[[Star Wars: Han Solo & Chewbacca]]'' to between around [[8 BBY]] and [[2 BBY]].</ref> Solo returned to Corellia on a mission to retrieve an urn containing the ashes of [[Krestrel D'Naran]] for Jabba.<ref name="Han Chewie 1" /> Upon arriving at a local bar, Solo encountered the criminal [[Corbus Tyra]], who posed as Ovan in order to collect the urn. Solo originally held doubts about the authenticity of the man's claim, though was convinced after he recounted the time Ovan had spoken to Han about the ships he built during his career.<ref name="Han Chewie 5">[[Han Solo & Chewbacca 5|''Han Solo & Chewbacca'' 5]]</ref>

