==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|Since so many SW characters are orphans or the product of some great tragedy, we wanted the story of Han's parentage to hint at something more complex and less romantic. His father led a working-class life, full of disappointment, and he had a complicated, difficult relationship with his son.|Jon Kasdan on Han's father|<ref name="Jon's Twitter">{{Twitter|JonKasdan|status/1040529505670946817|[[Jon Kasdan]]|quote=continued|archivefile=File:Jon-Kasdan-SoloFacts-September-14-2018.png}}</ref>}}
Ovan was first mentioned, albeit indirectly, in the [[2015]] reference book ''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars">''[[Ultimate Star Wars]]''</ref> He was first identified in the [[Han Solo & Chewbacca 1|first issue]] of the [[Star Wars comic books|comic]] miniseries ''[[Star Wars: Han Solo & Chewbacca]]'' written by [[Marc Guggenheim]],<ref name="Han Chewie 1" /> and published on [[March 9]], [[2022]].<ref name="Marvel">{{Marvel|url=comics/issue/96849/star_wars_han_solo_chewbacca_2022_1|text=Star Wars: Han Solo & Chewbacca (2022) #1}}</ref> He later made his first appearance, via a flashback, in the [[Han Solo & Chewbacca 2|second issue]] of the series,<ref name="Han Chewie 2" /> that was published on [[May 18]], 2022.<ref name="Marvel 2">{{Marvel|url=comics/issue/96850/star_wars_han_solo_chewbacca_2022_2|text=Star Wars: Han Solo & Chewbacca (2022) #2}}</ref> In [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]], the character was identified as [[Jonash Solo]].<ref name="TCoPL">''[[The Courtship of Princess Leia]]''</ref>

In [[November]] [[1977]], ''[[Star Wars]]'' creator [[George Lucas]] came up with Han Solo's backstory during story conferences he had with [[Leigh Brackett]] over the development of the story for the [[1980]] film [[Star Wars: Episode V The Empire Strikes Back|''Star Wars'': Episode V ''The Empire Strikes Back'']]. Lucas' backstory indirectly involved Han's father, being that Han had been orphaned on and raised by [[Wookiee]]s at [[Kashyyyk|their planet]] before befriending [[Chewbacca]].<ref name="The Star Wars Archives: Episodes I–III, 1999–2005">''[[The Star Wars Archives: Episodes I–III, 1999–2005]]''</ref> The first prominent mention of Han Solo's father came with the [[2018]] [[Star Wars Anthology Series|''Star Wars'' Anthology]] film ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''.<ref name="Solo" /> Solo's relationship with his father, as part of the film's backstory, was inspired by that of songwriter-musician [[Wikipedia:Bruce Springsteen|Bruce Springsteen]] with his father Douglas, as writers [[Jon Kasdan|Jon]] and [[Lawrence Kasdan]] both read Springteen's [[2016]] autobiography [[Wikipedia:Born to Run (autobiography)|''Born to Run'']] around the time they were writing the film's script.<ref name="Inspiration">{{WebCite|url=https://ultimateclassicrock.com/bruce-springsteen-solo-a-star-wars-story|text=Bruce Springsteen Inspired 'Solo: A Star Wars Story' Plot Point|author=Lifton, Dave|date=2018-05-25|work=Ultimate Classic Roc|archivedate=20200723132657}}</ref>

There are inconsistencies regarding the fate of Ovan. ''Ultimate Star Wars'' and its [[2019]] [[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition|updated edition]] both state that Han was orphaned at a young age, indirectly indicating that his father died.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /><ref name="Ultimate Star Wars New Edition">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> [[Mur Lafferty]]'s [[Solo: A Star Wars Story: Expanded Edition|novelization]] of ''Solo'' later stated that Ovan had abandoned Han.<ref name="Solo Expanded Edition" /> Jon Kasdan stated on [[Wikipedia:Twitter|Twitter]] that he believes that Han ran away from his father and that Han's father is still alive somewhere, drinking himself to death, however.<ref name="Jon's Twitter" /> ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' later confirmed his death.<ref name="Timelines" />

